From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wangzlei <66336933+wangzlei@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:02:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] exp: default eBPF config: context_propagation
 tcp_service_name

Servers return their service.name to the client in a TCP option (kind 26,
adot-obi patch 01), only to peers inside the VPC; the same as the obi receiver
default. No trace context (kind 25) and no HTTP traceparent header injection, so
the application payload is never modified; RED metrics and peer.service.name
topology are unchanged. Same change as adot-obi config/otel.yaml.
---
 packaging/dependencies/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ebpf.yaml | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packaging/dependencies/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ebpf.yaml b/packaging/dependencies/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ebpf.yaml
index 51206830..3832974f 100644
--- a/packaging/dependencies/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ebpf.yaml
+++ b/packaging/dependencies/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ebpf.yaml
@@ -26,8 +26,11 @@ receivers:
     log_level: INFO
     ebpf:
       bpf_fs_base_dir: /sys/fs/bpf
-      # Pinned: cwagent's obi receiver defaults to "tcp".
-      context_propagation: "all"
+      # Servers return their service.name to the client in a TCP option (kind 26,
+      # patch 01) -> peer.service.name; also cwagent's obi receiver default. Only
+      # to peers inside the VPC unless tcp_service_name_outside_vpc: true. No trace
+      # context and no HTTP header injection: the application payload is never modified.
+      context_propagation: "tcp_service_name"
       # false (OBI's default): a server request ends when its response is complete.
       # true submits it at the first response write, which dropped ~31% of
       # requests whose downstream calls were slow or timed out (ping demo, 2026-10-09).
-- 
